(Bug #131, position 2: `Write <call> to <file>` writes the text the call
 returns. It used to write nothing and set no error flag.)

To greeting.
    a text called words is "hello from a function".
    Return a text, words.

a text called 'log path' is "/tmp/vox_test_771_write_call.txt".
open a file for writing called 'the log' at 'log path'.
Write greeting to 'the log'.
On error Print "write flagged".
Print 'the log's size.
Write "{greeting}!" to 'the log'.
Print 'the log's size.
close 'the log'.

a buffer called readback is 64 bytes in size.
open a file for reading called 'saved' at 'log path'.
read from 'saved' into readback.
Print readback.
close 'saved'.
Delete the file 'log path'.
